WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.460
In September 2007, savers
queued outside a British bank,

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.690
trying to take their money out.

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.390
The money they had deposited
was not all sitting in a vault.

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.630
Banks keep only a fraction
of deposits as reserves.

5
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.610
And every loan they make
earns them interest.

6
00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.520
So when a bank lends you money,

7
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.130
whose money are you actually borrowing?

8
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.370
In this mission, you'll open
up a bank's balance sheet:

9
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.860
what it owns, and what it owes.

10
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.860
Then you'll change the
reserve ratio in a graph lab,

11
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.550
and watch what happens round by round.

12
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.520
Your mission: track where the
money in a loan really comes from.
